### 11. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

Implement server-enforced role-based access control.

**Resident**

- Manage their own profile.
- Create requests.
- View only their own requests and permitted attachments.
- Upload required corrections.
- View their notifications and request history.

**Request Processor / Barangay Staff**

- View assigned or otherwise authorized requests.
- Review information and attachments.
- Request corrections.
- Update permitted workflow statuses.
- Add internal notes where authorized.

**Barangay Secretary / Authorized Approving Official**

- Review requests within their assigned authority.
- Approve or reject requests.
- Authorize document preparation and release according to official procedures.
- View authorized operational reports.

**System Administrator**

- Manage staff accounts and permissions.
- Configure document services and system settings.
- Manage system-wide operational functions.
- View audit logs according to authorized responsibilities.

Use an explicitly defined permission matrix. Do not automatically grant every staff member unrestricted access.

Role assignments must be managed by authorized administrators or a trusted provisioning process, never by a public registration form.

### 12. DOCUMENT PREPARATION AND RELEASE

Create a document preparation module.

Allow authorized personnel to:

- Select an approved document template.
- Populate approved fields using verified request information.
- Preview the generated document.
- Print or download a draft for review.
- Record the required verification and approval steps.
- Mark a document as ready for release only after the necessary authorization.
- Record the date, method, and authorized staff member involved in release.

Use printable layouts appropriate for official barangay documents.

The system must not automatically create an apparently official, approved, signed, or sealed certificate merely because an online request was submitted.

Only authorized personnel may finalize official documents. Digital signatures, official seals, and QR-based verification must only be used when approved and implemented according to applicable requirements.

If PDF generation is supported by the development environment, implement it; otherwise, provide a reliable print-ready document workflow and clearly identify the remaining PDF integration.

### 13. NOTIFICATION SYSTEM

